  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "The dark editorial system, restrained cyan/red/yellow palette, bordered panels, and ROI focal graphic are cohesive across viewports. However, the desktop hero is compositionally unbalanced by a very large empty right field and awkward headline wrapping. Mobile compresses the ledger into tiny, crowded type—especially long row labels and currency values—while secondary labels and explanatory copy are frequently too faint. The global header is polished but visually cramped: desktop navigation approaches clipping, and tablet/mobile hide destinations behind a subtle “More” treatment.",
    "fix": "Rebalance the desktop hero into a deliberate two-column composition, tighten headline line breaks, and redesign the mobile ledger as stacked metric pairs instead of a squeezed table. Increase contrast and minimum size for secondary text, and make the header’s overflow/navigation state more visually explicit.",
